From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] binio: keep float conversion storage alive through byte output

The fixed 1.5 source stores pointers to outf/outd or buf declared inside
the conversion branch, then reads them in the byte-output loop after that
scope has ended. This is a generic C++ lifetime defect, not RISC-V assembly
or a QEMU limitation. Target CI 38646644683, head 6a384f55, fails the
unchanged downstream ieee-single-bytes check with normal -O2 flags.

Move the storage declarations to the enclosing IEEE block. Keep the
conversion, endian handling, default features and test assertions intact.
Preserve total source line count so the literal borrowed notice extraction
remains at its original lines. Remove after an official release contains
an equivalent lifetime fix. This is an original downstream patch; no
upstream submission or acceptance is claimed.

--- a/src/binio.cpp
+++ b/src/binio.cpp
@@ -396,11 +396,12 @@
     unsigned int	i, size;
     Byte		*out;
     bool		swap;
+    float	outf = f;
+    double	outd = f;
+    Byte	buf[8];
 
     if(system_flags & FloatIEEE) {
       // compatible system, let the hardware do the conversion
-      float	outf = f;
-      double	outd = f;
 
       // Hardware could be big or little endian, convert appropriately
       swap = getFlag(BigEndian) ^ (system_flags & BigEndian);
@@ -413,7 +414,6 @@
     } else {
 #if BINIO_WITH_MATH
       // incompatible system, do the conversion manually
-      Byte	buf[8];
 
       // Our own value is always big endian, just check whether we have to
       // convert for a different stream format.
